Inbound Processing

Entry Point
	•	Cloud Function: simulate_inbound_email
	•	Trigger: HTTP request or SendGrid inbound webhook

Responsibilities
	•	Extract RFQ ID from email subject
	•	Parse supplier details from email body:
	•	Supplier Name
	•	Unit Price
	•	Delivery Days
	•	Validate input format
	•	Support optional document reference via GCS URI


Processing Layer

RFQ Parsing

Structured data is extracted from unstructured email content using regular expressions.

Risk Scoring

Risk is calculated based on pricing and delivery timelines:

Condition	Score
Unit Price > 150000	+30
Unit Price < 80000	+25
Delivery Days > 30	+40
Delivery Days > 15	+20



Storage Layer

Cloud Storage (GCS)

Bucket: supplier-onboarding-risk

Stores:
	•	RFQ payloads (JSON format)
	•	Supplier documents (e.g., W-9 PDFs)

Acts as the raw data storage layer.

Data Layer

BigQuery Tables

RFQ Table
Stores transactional procurement data:
	•	rfq_id
	•	supplier_id
	•	supplier_name
	•	unit_price
	•	delivery_days
	•	risk_score
	•	quotation_gcs_uri
	•	created_at

W-9 Supplier Data (Planned)
Future integration with Document AI will enable structured extraction of supplier data:
	•	rfq_id
	•	supplier_name
	•	tax_id
	•	address
	•	document_gcs_uri
	•	created_at

Outbound Communication

SendGrid Integration

The system sends automated responses based on business logic:

Scenario	Action
High risk RFQ	Send negotiation email
Acceptable RFQ	Send confirmation email
Missing data	Request clarification

Implementation
	•	SendGrid API is used for transactional email delivery
	•	API keys should be managed using environment variables or Secret Manager

